w is  one of the actresses speaking out  against this deception in Tinseltown in  an interview with People magazine she  revealed that she was miffed about how  photoshopped she and her cast mates were  in promotional photos of Pretty Little  Liars she said nobody looked like  themselves she shared her frustrations  saying that even for magazine covers  they would Photoshop out imperfections  make her chest bigger her waist four  sizes smaller and made it so she didn't  even recognize herself she said she  never knew what to expect because she  had no control over the photo editing  process now she insists that  photographers not Photoshop photos aside  for minor touch-ups she sent out a  message to her young female fans not to  get down on themselves  she said that unless they announce that  a photo is not photoshopped it's  definitely photoshopped  she also reminded everyone that it takes  a lot of good lighting and makeup to  look like that the truth is no one looks  like that in real life  the transphobic plot twist after much  enticing mystery and anticipation PLL  finally delivered the big a reveal in  season six everyone was on the edge of  their seats but nearly filled to the  floor when the show dropped the  transgender bombshell who was his  character they revealed who had  tormented the liars during the course of  the story none other than the [ __ ]  characters CC which is short for  Charlotte Drake who was born as a boy  named Charles the trans community didn't  take too kindly to this as they believe  it contributes to a narrative in the  media that all trans people are  psychotic killers according to a  feminist online magazine this trope  appears in films like psycho and Silence  of the Lambs and TV shows like Law &amp;  Order SVU and CSI this does little to  create understanding and tolerance for  the trans community fans were less than  enthusiastic about this plot twist  showrunner Marlene King defended the  choice to make the murderer trans by  saying she didn't want people to think  that this person was a villain because  of their gender identity  she said Stacy was a villain because she  came from a very crazy family and was  therefore genetically predisposed to  insanity she expressed that it was not  her intent to go backwards for the trans  community she wanted to go forward fans  hated the ending Pretty Little Liars had  a loyal fan following for seven seasons  but they had to deal with some angry  backlash after the final episode reveal  the series finale solved the mystery by  exposing the mastermind behind all the  pretty girl head games as Spencer's  super psycho British twin sister Alex  Drake and she is of course wearing the  same exact outfit as Spencer making for  the cliched conundrum which twin do I  shoot and then there's Jenna on a horse  fans were less than pleased these peeved  pretty fans took to Twitter to unleash  their discontent saying things like so  it took them and us seven years figuring  out who ad was and a horse and Jenna  Marshall can do it in seconds and that  they spent years watching PLL only to be  given an evil twin with a bad accent and  a horse that's a better detective than  all of them they also cited the horse as  the smartest character and Pretty Little  Liars tough crowd  then there were the fans that had a lot  of unanswered questions such as why Mia  was mentioned or how did Alex kill Wren  and how did the moms escape the overall  consensus is that fans lost seven years  of their lives invested in the show and  they want that time back Pretty Little  Liars spinoff  you probably know that Marlene King is  adapting the book series the  perfectionists to a new TV show on  freeform here are some intriguing  secrets we uncovered so far we know that  Sasha Pieterse and Janel Parrish will  return as their PLL characters Alison  DiLaurentis and mode a Vander Waal but  they will be in a new town with new  mysteries and a brand new murder so are  there any of the other characters from  Pretty Little Liars going to make an  appearance Sasha let it slip then it  won't be a problem at all to get Shay  Mitchell on the show  it's unclear how big her role will be  however don't get your hopes up that you  will see the return of all your favorite  PLL characters Lucy Hale revealed that  she doesn't think she will be in the  spinoff she said since its filming in  Vancouver she might go and stop the set  of it showrunner Marlene King shared  that she plans to deviate from the book  in a few ways she revealed plans to  focus more on the male characters  Marlene also revealed that not all four  of the main characters will survive the  first episode is the first victim going  to be a guy what do you think somebody  get the popcorn and that's it for ten  dark secrets in Pretty Little Liars  thanks for watching the things see you  next time  [Music]
 

